{%- comment -%}
  THP horizontal logo lockup — icon on the left, wordmark on the right.

  Replaces the single stacked logo image. The mark is an image; the wordmark is
  live text by default rather than a second image, which is both sharper at
  every size and readable by search engines and screen readers. A wordmark image
  can still be supplied and takes over when set.

  The mark's alt is intentionally empty: the shop name sits right beside it as
  real text, so giving the image an alt as well would make a screen reader
  announce the brand twice for one link.

  Accepts:
    mark      {image}  icon shown on the left
    wordmark  {image}  optional image wordmark; replaces the text when set
    name      {string} wordmark text (falls back to shop.name)
    tagline   {string} optional small line under the name
    fallback  {image}  legacy single-image logo, used when no mark is set
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign hp_mark = mark | default: fallback
  assign hp_name = name | default: shop.name
-%}

<span class="hp-logo">
  {%- if hp_mark != blank -%}
    <span class="hp-logo__mark">
      {{
        hp_mark
        | image_url: width: 400
        | image_tag: class: 'hp-logo__mark-img', widths: '80, 120, 200, 300, 400', alt: '', preload: true
      }}
    </span>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if wordmark != blank -%}
    <span class="hp-logo__type hp-logo__type--image">
      {{ wordmark | image_url: width: 900 | image_tag: class: 'hp-logo__type-img', widths: '200, 400, 600, 900', alt: hp_name }}
    </span>
  {%- elsif hp_name != blank -%}
    <span class="hp-logo__type">
      <span class="hp-logo__name">{{ hp_name }}</span>
      {%- if tagline != blank -%}
        <span class="hp-logo__tag">{{ tagline }}</span>
      {%- endif -%}
    </span>
  {%- endif -%}
</span>
